Foxconn Changes Its Virtualization System
​Foxconn has stopped using VMware for some of its computer systems.
​The company has chosen a different platform called ArcRfra.
​Foxconn says the new system will run many workloads, including AI.
​The company wants a platform that is flexible and easy to grow.
​Many businesses are looking at new choices instead of VMware.
​They want lower costs and more control over their systems.
​Changing a virtualization platform is a big job.
​It takes careful planning, testing, and training.
​Foxconn believes the new platform will support its future AI projects.
​The writer says more companies may look for new virtualization tools as the market continues to change.
